{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetH7hnpAYgszyqcWnQSo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository already has:**\n\n1. **Error handling pattern**: Exceptions are used to signal API failures\n   - `ConflictException` throws HTTP 409 with an error code (see `ShipmentController.kt:29`)\n   - `ResourceNotFoundException` throws HTTP 404 with an error code (see `ShipmentController.kt:49`)\n   - All errors use the error envelope: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [] } }` (see `ApiError.kt`)\n\n2. **Test pattern** (per testing-and-verification skill):\n   - Assertions check response body, not just status\n   - After state-changing calls, re-read the resource through a separate GET\n   - After refusals, re-read to assert no change occurred\n   - Error assertions check `error.code`, not just status\n\n3. **Controller pattern**: \n   - `@PostMapping` for create, `@GetMapping` for read, with `@PathVariable` and `@RequestBody`\n   - Return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(...)` for creation (see `ShipmentController.kt:43`)\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. **ShipmentController.kt** — Must add the `confirm` endpoint (idempotent, handles CONFIRMED/CANCELLED/not-found cases)\n2. **ApiError.kt** — Must add a new `ErrorCode` for rejecting CANCELLED shipments (defensive; helps tests assert on code)\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Must add tests for the confirm endpoint, including state verification through separate GETs\n\n**Risks:**\n\n1. Forgetting to make the confirm call idempotent (must not fail on CONFIRMED)\n2. Not using the correct HTTP status (409 for CANCELLED, 404 for missing)\n3. Not persisting the state change (update must call `repository.save()`)\n4. Breaking existing tests if the implementation is wrong\n\n**Open questions:** None. The ticket clearly specifies all four cases and their expected outcomes.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add a new `ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_FOR_CONFIRM` to the enum. This allows tests to assert that CANCELLED shipments are rejected with a specific code (409 Conflict).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` endpoint that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID; if not found, throws `ResourceNotFoundException` (404)\n   - If status is `CANCELLED`, throws `ConflictException` with the new error code (409)\n   - If status is `CREATED`, sets it to `CONFIRMED` and saves it\n   - If status is `CONFIRMED`, does nothing (idempotent)\n   - Returns the shipment (whether changed or not) with HTTP 200\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four tests:\n   - **Test 1**: Confirms a CREATED shipment → assert response body contains CONFIRMED, verify state through separate GET\n   - **Test 2**: Re-confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment → assert it succeeds and returns the same state\n   - **Test 3**: Attempts to confirm a CANCELLED shipment → assert 409 with error code, verify shipment is unchanged\n   - **Test 4**: Attempts to confirm a non-existent shipment → assert 404 with error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- *Creating a separate `ShipmentService` layer*: The existing `ShipmentController` directly uses the repository and throws exceptions in-place. Adding a service layer would deviate from the convention and is unnecessary for the small amount of logic required (state check + save). The ticket forbids new dependencies anyway, so staying in the controller is the right choice.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Flow | Read | Write | Response |\n|------|------|------|-------|----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | GET repo, status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED, save, return | `repository.findById(shipmentId)` | `repository.save(shipment with CONFIRMED)` | 200 + updated shipment |\n| CONFIRMED (retry) | GET repo, status is CONFIRMED, no change, save same state, return | `repository.findById(shipmentId)` | `repository.save(shipment with CONFIRMED)` | 200 + same shipment |\n| CANCELLED | GET repo, status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException | `repository.findById(shipmentId)` | (none) | 409 + error envelope |\n| Not found | GET repo returns null, throw ResourceNotFoundException | `repository.findById(shipmentId)` | (none) | 404 + error envelope |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n| Test | Case | Assertions |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| confirm_created_to_confirmed | CREATED → CONFIRMED | 1. Status code 200, 2. Response body status = CONFIRMED, 3. Separate GET returns CONFIRMED |\n| confirm_already_confirmed_idempotent | CONFIRMED (retry) | 1. Status code 200, 2. Response body unchanged, 3. Separate GET returns same state |\n| confirm_cancelled_rejected | CANCELLED | 1. Status code 409, 2. Error code = SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_FOR_CONFIRM, 3. Separate GET shows CANCELLED unchanged |\n| confirm_not_found | Non-existent | 1. Status code 404, 2. Error code = SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1131,"cache_read_input_tokens":16096,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1131},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d046e827-0023-4e35-b5ca-0c9426d3e838","uuid":"8cd02b59-5082-4255-837d-d4e83279ed0f","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:42:56.563Z","request_id":"req_011CetH7h9c5UG1DHHxUriC5"}
