tion file changes** — Only ShipmentController.kt and ApiError.kt modified (both required for the feature)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n| File | Change | Justification |\n|------|--------|---------------|\n| **ApiError.kt** | Added `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_FOR_CONFIRM` to ErrorCode enum | Required to distinguish the CANCELLED rejection case from other 409s; allows tests to assert on the error code |\n| **ShipmentController.kt** | Added `confirm()` method with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` | Core endpoint implementation; handles CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotent on CONFIRMED, rejects CANCELLED (409) and missing (404) |\n| **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** | Added 4 test methods | Required per testing-and-verification skill: each case (CREATED, CONFIRMED retry, CANCELLED, missing) has a test; each state-changing test re-reads via separate GET; error cases assert on error code |\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are met, all existing tests pass, no new dependencies, no unrelated files modified.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm to move shipments from CREATED to CONFIRMED, idempotent on CONFIRMED, rejecting CANCELLED with 409 and missing with 404.\n\nChanged       ApiError.kt — Added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_FOR_CONFIRM error code for rejecting CANCELLED shipments\n              ShipmentController.kt — Added confirm() endpoint that transitions CREATED→CONFIRMED, is idempotent on CONFIRMED, rejects CANCELLED/missing\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — Added 4 tests covering CREATED confirmation, CONFIRMED idempotency, CANCELLED rejection, and missing rejection\n\nTests         confirm_created_to_confirmed — Confirms CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED and persists\n              confirm_already_confirmed_idempotent — Retry confirm on CONFIRMED succeeds without change (idempotent)\n              rejects_confirm_on_cancelled_shipment_with_error_envelope — Attempt to confirm CANCE